WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:03.420
[The sound of strong winds]

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:09.092
The wind is making it extremely uncomfortably cold

00:00:09.092 --> 00:00:13.220
It is probably between -10 and -15 [degrees celcius]

00:00:13.804 --> 00:00:16.432
We just had -27 a couple of weeks ago

00:00:16.432 --> 00:00:20.018
In general when the wind picks up
it's really really cold

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:22.228
My name is Andreas
My name is Johannes

00:00:22.228 --> 00:00:25.565
I'm in Norway
I'm on the Field Quality Engineering team

00:00:25.565 --> 00:00:28.234
 just a couple of kilometers below the Arctic Circle

00:00:33.446 --> 00:00:36.991
This week we're gonna take a Model Y through Norway

00:00:36.991 --> 00:00:42.496
and see how it performs on a customer level 
 and customer expectations

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.501
Testing is important because we can predict 
 what the customer will experience

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:50.962
when they are actually driving here

00:00:51.629 --> 00:00:53.964
The weather can be super local around here

00:00:53.964 --> 00:00:56.425
We have no crosswinds at all right now

00:00:56.425 --> 00:01:01.846
and then three kilometers down the road 
 you suddenly have 40 km/h crosswinds

00:01:02.847 --> 00:01:05.641
So it's a very common scenario for Norway

00:01:05.641 --> 00:01:08.227
where people live in the city close by the Sea

00:01:08.227 --> 00:01:12.522
and then basically go up to the mountain 
 to their cabins over the weekend

00:01:12.522 --> 00:01:16.317
The water that accumulates around the car

00:01:16.317 --> 00:01:20.780
maybe around the wipers
 or around the wheels will tend to freeze

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:25.242
and we still need to have a car 
 that performs well under those conditions

00:01:26.547 --> 00:01:29.746
[Calm music]

00:01:32.378 --> 00:01:35.042
[The sound of squeaking snow]

00:01:40.547 --> 00:01:42.132
That it's slippery

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.846
We're trying to replicate customer scenarios

00:01:48.846 --> 00:01:54.184
and finding all the challenges with driving a car 
 in the northern Scandinavian parts

00:01:54.184 --> 00:02:00.648
For this trip we have equipped taillights 
 with a humidity temperature and pressure sensor

00:02:00.648 --> 00:02:03.859
to measure what the interior of the light actually withstands

00:02:03.859 --> 00:02:07.696
during the mountain climbs 
 and the tunnel temperature differences

00:02:07.696 --> 00:02:10.949
Lasse actually made a super good simple setup

00:02:10.949 --> 00:02:14.660
which I think is one of the strengths 
 of the Field Quality Engineering team

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:16.787
that we can do a lot with little

00:02:18.872 --> 00:02:21.458
[Calm music continues]

00:02:26.588 --> 00:02:30.299
Now we're for a brief moment in the workshop

00:02:30.328 --> 00:02:35.220
to inspect a couple of things 
 that is difficult to do alongside the road

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:40.850
and we try to do it quickly 
 to not dry or heat up the car too much

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:44.561
because we want to have it outside as much as we can

00:02:44.561 --> 00:02:48.982
Now I'm inspecting the the wiper washer hoses

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:55.446
The typical day up here 
is a very harsh environment for the cars

00:02:55.446 --> 00:03:00.033
because you have a lot of temperature differences 
 as well as elevation changes

00:03:00.033 --> 00:03:03.036
so you can really stress the car in this area

00:03:03.036 --> 00:03:06.622
simulating a complete winter in a couple of weeks

00:03:06.873 --> 00:03:12.211
This testing hopefully means that we can increase 
 durability and reliability of our product

00:03:12.211 --> 00:03:16.881
and that it will work in any scenario 
 anywhere in the world

00:03:18.466 --> 00:03:21.219
[Upbeat music]

